{
  "id": "bigwig-table",
  "measured": "2026-09-28",
  "published": false,
  "source": {
    "kind": "bench",
    "repro": "node plugins/marks/benches/bigwigPaths.bench.ts --file=HG008_log2ratio.500bp.bw --refName=chr1 --screenPx=400000 --zooms=600,2500 --rounds=9 --json, and again with --no-index",
    "notes": "On ada, over a 54 MB 500 bp-bin BigWig (a copy-number log2 ratio from the GIAB HG008 cancer set), one 400,000 px screen of chr1 at 600 and 2500 bp/px so a region holds 10^5-10^6 rows; bbi's block cache is warm, so each arm is a refetch over held blocks plus what its RPC executor does. Wiggle is getFeatureArraysMulti and processFeaturesFromArrays; features is getFeaturesArray (a BigWigFeature per row) and encodeFeatures over the bar's lanes; table is getFeatureTable, a ColumnTable over bbi's arrays, and the same encode. A bar asks for the hit index; the declined rows leave it out, which wiggle's hover does without. MIN across rounds, x, x2 and y checked equal across the three before timing."
  },
